{
  "name": "geneva-montblanc",
  "notes": "Lake Geneva basin (Geneva at the west end) to the Mont Blanc massif, sized for a 50 x 50 cm frame: 2x2 tiles of 245 mm at 1:200,000 = 49 km per tile, 98 x 98 km total. Bands: water, two vegetation tiers, rock, snow. No shore band (dropped 2026-09-28: at this scale it is a 1-2 mm rim that cost most of the manual swaps). 5 colours on 4 slots: palette.overflow='swap' plans a manual swap on tiles that reach the snowline; set 'merge' to auto-merge the two least distinct bands instead. Exaggeration fixed at 2.0x (2026-09-28) so the tallest tile is ~49 mm and fits a 6 cm deep frame under glass; auto would pick 2.5x (60 mm).",
